  "subject": "A left-handed woman and right-handed boyfriend whose elbows knocked all through their first date at a seven-stool ramen counter; now she always sits on his left so they can eat and hold hands, and when only the wrong seats are free, both eat wrong-handed.",
  "caption": "Mandarin retro kayokyoku pop in the 1970s Taiwanese ballad style with a light rumba lilt. Nylon-string guitar arpeggios, legato string section with answering counter-lines, tremolo mandolin fills between vocal phrases, round electric bass on root and fifth, brushed drums with rim-clicks. Warm vintage studio mix with plate reverb. Female vocal, sweet clear mid-register in full voice with gentle vibrato and small ornamental turns at line ends. Clear full voice, every word enunciated, steady sung melody on every line. 88 BPM, G major. Sweet, shy, contented mood. No rap, no autotune, no electronic drums, no synth bass, no whispered or crooned delivery.",
  "lyrics": "[Intro - nylon guitar, mandolin, strings]\n\n[Verse 1]\n拉麵店只有七張板凳\n我們第一次約會\n你的右手 我的左手\n筷子打架 手肘也碰到\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\n你說對不起 我說沒關係\n麵都涼了 臉卻很熱\n\n[Chorus]\n你坐我右邊 我坐你左邊\n這樣就能 牽著手吃麵\n你坐我右邊 慢慢吃不急\n湯是熱的 手也是\n\n[Verse 2]\n後來每次排隊進去\n我先看哪裡有空位\n老闆笑著指一指\n我們走向 靠牆那兩張\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\n有一天座位被占了\n只剩你左邊我右邊\n\n[Chorus]\n你坐我右邊 我坐你左邊\n這樣就能 牽著手吃麵\n你坐我右邊 換手也不怕\n兩個人 都用錯手\n\n[Chorus]\n你坐我右邊 我坐你左邊\n這樣就能 牽著手吃麵\n你坐我右邊 慢慢吃不急\n湯是熱的 手更熱\n\n[Outro - nylon guitar, strings fade]\n下次我還坐你左邊",
